    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0397" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2357</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-27T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1918,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 27, 3.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In reply to Russian Minister’s inquiry as to the position this Legation would
                    take in regard to the recommendation of the Allied <pb facs="0398" n="308"
                        xml:id="pg308"/> consuls at Vladivostok that General Horvat be advised not to proceed to Vladivostok unless
                    as a private citizen or chief of the railway, I stated that under my
                    instructions, I did not feel competent to express any views in regard to the
                    political activities of General Horvat
                    or of any other faction in Siberia. In view of the suspicions of a monarchical
                    tendency in his movement, does the Department desire any modification of this
                    attitude?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >MacMurray</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
